SUMMARY:Lunch and Learn: Tokenomics 101
DESCRIPTION:All Things AI (Live)\nLeaders across industries are moving fas
 t on AI\, but very few can explain why the bill keeps climbing while the p
 lan price stays the same. That gap is tokenomics\, and it is quietly shapi
 ng what AI actually costs your team.\n\nIn this Lunch and Learn\, Don Shin
 \, CEO of CrossComm\, breaks down how these tools bill by consumption\, wh
 y prompt bloat drives spend without anyone noticing\, and the concrete hab
 its that stretch a paid plan or a free tier a lot further. You will walk =
  away able to see where your money goes and how to get more out of every d
 ollar you put into AI.\n\nTokenomics 101: Spending With Intention on AI As
  organizations adopt AI agents\, token consumption and the AI bills that r
 esult have been increasing sharply: agentic workflows can make 10 to 20 ti
 mes more model calls per run than a single chat interaction. The answer fo
 r users and organizations who wish to remain AI-forward is to learn the di
 scipline of spending tokens deliberately.\n\nThis webinar will present a b
 rief primer on tokenomics across three horizons: matching model class to t
 ask in the near term\, graduating repeatable agent work into deterministic
  code in the mid term\, and owning your harness and model selection in the
  long term to achieve cost control\,\nprivacy\, and AI sovereignty.\n\nWha
 t You Will Learn\n\n1\\. What a token actually is\\\, and how AI tools bil
 l you for them\n2\\. Why your costs rise even when the subscription price 
 holds steady\n3\\. The difference between a bloated prompt and a tight one
 \n4\\. Three habits that stretch a paid plan or a free tier further\n5\\. 
 How to pick the right model for the job instead of overpaying for every ta
 sk
